# CODEOWNERS
# Practice: P9 Collaboration (Tier 1, 36 mentions)
#           P11 Code review  (Tier 1, 33 mentions)
#
# Named owners per area make review a structural requirement rather than a
# favour. Combined with branch protection ("Require review from Code Owners"),
# this is the mechanism that evidences both practices.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# !! PLACEHOLDER — REPLACE BEFORE ENABLING "Require review from Code Owners"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub silently ignores usernames that do not exist or are not collaborators,
# which produces a file that LOOKS like a control but enforces nothing. Verify
# after replacing:  gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/codeowners/errors
#
# Replace the four placeholders below with real GitHub usernames:
#   @OWNER-MOHAMED   -> Mohamed Elkhanfaf (repository owner)
#   @MEMBER-2        -> teammate 2
#   @MEMBER-3        -> teammate 3
#   @MEMBER-4        -> teammate 4
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                           @OWNER-MOHAMED

# ---- Security-critical paths: owner review always required ----------------
# Changes here can silently disable a control, so they are deliberately
# routed to the person accountable for the pipeline.

/.github/                   @OWNER-MOHAMED
/.github/workflows/         @OWNER-MOHAMED
/.gitleaks.toml             @OWNER-MOHAMED
/.pre-commit-config.yaml    @OWNER-MOHAMED
/SECURITY.md                @OWNER-MOHAMED
/.gitignore                 @OWNER-MOHAMED

# Authentication, authorization and cryptography are the highest-risk code in
# the project. Two-person review is the intent here.
/backend/src/auth/          @OWNER-MOHAMED @MEMBER-2
/backend/src/middleware/    @OWNER-MOHAMED @MEMBER-2

# ---- Feature areas --------------------------------------------------------

/backend/                   @MEMBER-2 @OWNER-MOHAMED
/frontend/                  @MEMBER-3
/backend/tests/             @MEMBER-3 @OWNER-MOHAMED

# Infrastructure, containers, monitoring
/docker/                    @MEMBER-4
/infra/                     @MEMBER-4 @OWNER-MOHAMED
/monitoring/                @MEMBER-4

# ---- Documentation --------------------------------------------------------
# Deliverables, so still reviewed — but not by the pipeline owner alone.

/docs/                      @MEMBER-4 @OWNER-MOHAMED
/docs/threat-model/         @OWNER-MOHAMED @MEMBER-4
/docs/adr/                  @OWNER-MOHAMED
/evidence/                  @OWNER-MOHAMED
/tasks/                     @OWNER-MOHAMED
